      "diff": "Looking at the incident, the issue is clear:\n\n1. A GET request to `/carts/ghost` fails with `KeyError: 'ghost'` at line 214\n2. The `get_cart` function tries to access `CARTS[cart_id]` directly without checking if the cart exists\n3. Other endpoints like `checkout` and `cart_tax` properly check `if cart_id not in CARTS` before accessing\n4. The previous patch was rejected because it tried to patch `main.py` which doesn't exist at that path\n\nThe root cause is that `get_cart` should validate the cart exists before attempting access, consistent with other endpoints. The path issue in the previous attempt suggests the file is in a subdirectory structure.\n\nBased on the traceback showing the file at `/private/var/folders/mv/mzz_q2mn3q3c827r6pfcby640000gn/T/main-N02-C3-s1-7lewco5b/live_alpha/alpha/main.py`, the correct relative path from repository root is `alpha/main.py`.\n\n--- a/alpha/main.py\n+++ b/alpha/main.py\n@@ -211,6 +211,8 @@ def add_to_cart(cart_id: str, item: dict) -> dict:\n \n @app.get(\"/carts/{cart_id}\")\n def get_cart(cart_id: str) -> dict:\n+    if cart_id not in CARTS:\n+        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=f\"no cart {cart_id}\")\n     items = CARTS[cart_id]\n     first = items[0][\"sku\"] if items else None\n     return {\"cart\": cart_id, \"size\": len(items), \"first_sku\": first}",
